Unjust damage to my creditworthiness. 
Emotional distress and financial hardship due to false and misleading information remaining on my credit report. 

Unlawful Reporting of Unauthorized Hard Inquiries : In addition to failing to investigate these accounts, I have also sent numerous disputes regarding the following XXXX hard inquiries that were made between XX/XX/XXXX and XX/XX/XXXX you improperly treated as individual hard inquiries rather than recognizing them as part of the 14-15 day window allowed by the FCRA for similar loan inquiries. 

XXXX XXXXDate of inquiry : XX/XX/XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXDate of inquiry : XX/XX/XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX  Date of inquiry : XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX of inquiry : XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX of inquiry : XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXDate of inquiry : XX/XX/XXXX Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and guidelines established by the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau XXXX CFPB ), credit reporting agencies ( CRAs ) such as yourself are required to combine multiple hard inquiries for the same type of loan when they occur within a specific rate-shopping period. 

Rate-Shopping Window and Inquiry Treatment : 1. 14-45 Day Window for Rate Shopping : For mortgage, auto, and student loans, multiple inquiries within a 14 to 45-day window are counted as a single inquiry for credit scoring purposes.

FICO Score Models : FICO models 5, 4, and 2 ( commonly used in mortgage lending ) apply a 14-day window.

Newer FICO models ( FICO 8 and 9 ) extend this window to 45 days.

VantageScore Model : VantageScore uses a 14-day window for combining inquiries.

2. Same Type of Loan Requirement : To qualify for combination, the inquiries must be for the same type of loan ( e.g., mortgage, auto, or student loan ). 
Applications for credit cards, personal loans, or other types of credit do not qualify for this treatment. 

The purpose of this provision is to allow consumers to shop for the best loan terms without being penalized by multiple hard inquiries that could otherwise lower their credit scores. The scoring models recognize that consumers XXXX apply with multiple lenders to compare rates, which is a financially responsible practice. 

